virtio_pci: poll the reset status without a timer-tick sleep

vp_reset() waits for the device to read back status 0. On
Virtualization.framework the first read is usually still nonzero, so
each device costs one msleep(1), which is two jiffies: 8 ms at HZ=250.
With eight virtio devices that is 65 ms of a 90 ms kernel boot.
Measured on a Mac mini M4, 2026-11-07.

--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_modern.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_pci_modern.c
@@ -556,7 +556,7 @@ static void vp_reset(struct virtio_device *vdev)
 	 * including MSI-X interrupts, if any.
 	 */
 	while (vp_modern_get_status(mdev))
-		msleep(1);
+		usleep_range(20, 100);

 	vp_modern_avq_cleanup(vdev);

